.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt SCREENCAPTURE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm screencapture
.Nd capture the screen to image files or the pasteboard
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cmx
.Op Fl D Ar display
.Op Fl l Ar windowid
.Op Fl R Ar x,y,w,h
.Op Fl t Ar format
.Op Fl T Ar seconds
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
captures what the window server shows: every active display, one of
them, a rectangle of the desktop, or one window, and writes it to image
files, one for each display captured, or to the general pasteboard.
.Bl -tag -width "-R x,y,w,h"
.It Fl c
Puts the capture on the general pasteboard (PNG and TIFF) instead of
writing files.
.It Fl D Ar display
Captures display number
.Ar display
only; 1 is the main display.
.It Fl l Ar windowid
Captures the window with this number only, as
.Xr wsctl 8
lists them.
.It Fl m
Captures the main display only.
.It Fl R Ar x,y,w,h
Captures a rectangle of the desktop, in points from the main display's
top left corner.
.It Fl t Ar format
The files' format:
.Cm png
(the default) or
.Cm tiff .
.It Fl T Ar seconds
Waits this long before capturing.
.It Fl x
Makes no sound (there is none yet).
.El
.Pp
Capturing other programs' windows is for the console's user and root.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
The main display to a PNG file, after three seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
screencapture -m -T 3 desktop.png
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pbcopy 1 ,
.Xr wsctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in Minkar 19.6.
.Sh BUGS
Interactive selection
.Pq Fl i , Fl w
and capturing the cursor
.Pq Fl C
are not available yet; those options are refused.
JPEG files
.Pq Fl t Cm jpg
are not written yet: the JPEG encoder is not built.
